Preorder Traversal = Root → Left → Right

We visit the nodes in this specific order:
1. Root: Visit the current node first.
2. Left: Traverse the entire left subtree.
3. Right: Traverse the entire right subtree.

Why push right first?
Because a Stack follows LIFO (Last In, First Out).

So, if we push:
- Right child first.
- Left child second.
The left child will come out first!
